# Workflow: Adding a New Feature

> Apply this checklist for every new feature or spec change. Check each step — do not skip.

## Checklist

### Before coding

- [ ] `npx speckit-ai start "<title>"` (or `--affects=<feature>` to change an existing feature)
- [ ] Write the spec in `specs/active/<name>/targets/<feature>.md` (structure from `specs/_template.md`)
- [ ] Resolve all Open Questions in the spec before implementing
- [ ] Create `plan.md` and `tasks.md` from the spec (tasks in 4 phases, Tests is mandatory)

### While coding

- [ ] Place files in the correct directory according to `docs/core-principles-and-coding-standards/structure.md`
- [ ] Follow patterns in `docs/core-principles-and-coding-standards/coding-conventions.md`
- [ ] Write unit tests for important logic (`npx speckit-ai generate tests` gives a skeleton per `AC-n`)
- [ ] Record architecture decisions with `npx speckit-ai generate adr "<title>"`

### Before reporting done

- [ ] `{{PACKAGE_MANAGER}} run lint` — must pass, no warnings
- [ ] `{{PACKAGE_MANAGER}} run test` — 100% pass
- [ ] All Acceptance Criteria in the spec checked off
- [ ] Create `review.md` summarizing what was done and lessons learned
- [ ] `npx speckit-ai lint`, then `npx speckit-ai done` (writes the spec to `specs/features/` and archives the work files)
